Z||000000||count_iblis||11-12-2000||09:54 PM||||I think I said that right, but anyway was is the purpose of a shift kit?  I was telling someone the idea I had about putting a 3.4 in the GT I have and I told him that I missed have a manual (My first auto ever and Im 27) and he said that a shift kit would be the idea thing for me to have.  I didnt want to go in depth with him about it since we were in the checkout line.  So Im asking my fellow fiero brothers here.  <P><BR>Thanks, <P><BR>Chris<P>------------------<BR>COUNTIBLIS <BR>"HUG YOUR KIDS SPANK THE SOUND BARRIER"||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-12-2000||11:21 PM||||Actually it's B&M and they don't make parts for TH125. You have to goto to <BR><A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A> or Fiero store or someone else.<P>It reprograms certain tranny functions. just what depends on the kit. makes the tranny shift faster between gears.<P>It doesn't make up for a tranny that's not adjusted right or damaged. It can hide some problems. You need to make sure the tranny is good before the kit goes in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-13-2000||10:19 AM||||I have a "Trans-Go" shift kit in mine. It is the same one sold thru IRM. It basically provides better shifting.<BR>There are some other changes you can do but it's all listed in the instructions. It's been awhile so I don't remember what they are but I did install the anti-bleed down for the torque converter. It helps keep the torque converter loaded with trans fluid during hard cornering. The anti-bleed down was actually used on the 2.8L Pontiac 6000 and chevy celebrity from the factory.<BR>For the roughly $40.00 it was worth it. As for how long it takes to install, A friend at a trans place did it in about an hour without removing the trans or engine.||||reg||1
